|passage=I was a young un at 'Oogli,<br>Shy as a girl to begin;<br>Aggie de Castrer she '''made''' me,<br>— An' Aggie was clever as sin;<br>Older than me, but my first un —<br>More like a mother she were<br>Showed me the way to promotion an' pay,<br>An' I learned about women from 'er!}}
